      "description": "Watch Rotherham United vs West Bromwich Albion highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. Rotherham United hosted West Bromwich Albion on 2026-08-08 in a highly anticipated Carabao Cup encounter. Both sides entered the match looking to establish early momentum and secure their place in the next round of the tournament. Clinical First Half from the Baggies West Bromwich Albion started the match with intent, applying pressure from the very first whistle. The breakthrough came early in the 8th minute when Jimmy-Jay Morgan reacted quickest to a blocked shot from Harry Whitwell , slotting the ball home from close range. The visitors continued to dominate proceedings, and their persistence paid off again in the 24th minute. Harry Whitwell , having already played a key role in the opener, found the top left corner with a powerful left-footed strike following an assist from Alex Mowatt . Rotherham United struggled to find their rhythm, though Paul Mullin and Jili Buyabu attempted to spark a comeback through quick transitions. However, the West Bromwich Albion defense remained disciplined, and goalkeeper Ted Cann had to be alert to keep the scoreline from widening further before the halftime break, making several crucial saves from long-range efforts. Second Half Dominance and Late Consolation The momentum remained firmly with the visitors after the interval. Substitute Felix Myhre made an immediate impact, extending the lead to 3-0 in the 55th minute with a composed finish into the top of the net. The clinical display continued in the 61st minute as Jimmy-Jay Morgan secured his second goal of the match, heading home a precise cross from Callum Styles . The goal essentially sealed the tie, allowing the visitors to manage the game through a series of substitutions. Despite the deficit, Rotherham United showed resilience in the closing stages. In the 87th minute, Fábio Tavares provided a moment of individual brilliance, firing a right-footed shot into the top left corner after being set up by Ar'Jany Martha . Although Tavares later received a yellow card in stoppage time for a foul on Nathaniel Phillips , the goal provided some cheer for the home supporters as the match concluded 4-1 in favor of a superior West Bromwich Albion side."
